  "src": "right pixel in each row whose two foreground colors are blue/teal or yellow/orange",
  "path": "leftward along the same row until immediately right of the other foreground pixel",
  "trajectory": "keep only the final pixel immediately right of the other foreground pixel",
  "transform": "erase the original right-pixel location; leave other two-pixel rows unchanged"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-10 rows x 4-10 cols, black background
  rows: each row is empty (all black) or contains exactly 2 distinct foreground pixels
  moving_pairs: blue/teal (1,8) and yellow/orange (4,7) — order within row is random
  distractor_pairs: any other 2-color combination (may include moving-family colors cross-paired, e.g. blue+yellow)
  row_counts:
    moving: 1-4
    distractor: 2-5
    empty: 0-2
    nonempty <= grid rows
  moving_gap: pixels separated by 1-7 empty cells (gap >= 1, so never already adjacent)
  distractor_gap: 1-6 empty cells between the two pixels
  transform: for each moving-pair row, slide the right pixel leftward to be adjacent to the left pixel; clear original position. Distractors and empty rows unchanged.

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid dimensions (rows, cols) within ranges.
    2. Decide how many moving rows (1-4), distractor rows (2-5), empty rows (0-2); total <= grid rows.
    3. Assign row types randomly (moving / distractor / empty).
    4. For each moving row, build the OUTPUT state first — pick a left-pixel column c0 (0..cols-3), place a random-order moving pair at (c0, c0+1). This is the compacted/adjacent output.
    5. To get the INPUT, pick c1 > c0+1 for the right pixel (gap 1-7 within bounds), move the right pixel from c0+1 to c1, leave c0+1 empty.
    6. For each distractor row, place 2 foreground pixels at random columns with gap >= 1; choose a color pair that is NOT a moving pair. Copy identically to both input and output.
    7. Verify no row has conflicting pixel placements (each cell holds at most one pixel).
```
